USAGE = """\
usage: scripts/mod/compare [--project brotli|re2|brotli-tidy|brotli-tidy-fail]... [--case GLOB]... [--blaze BIN]
                           [--side oracle|blaze|both|none] [--list] [--show NAME]
                           [--json FILE]
       scripts/mod/compare selftest
       scripts/mod/compare help

Runs a fixed list of `mod` invocations (dump_repo_mapping, show_repo, graph, deps, all_paths,
path, explain, show_extension, tidy and their error cases) with the oracle
(~/.cache/blaze/oracle/bazel-9.3.2-linux-x86_64) and with Blaze (--blaze, default
target/debug/blaze) on work copies of the corpus projects (and of two fixtures, brotli-tidy and brotli-tidy-fail:
brotli plus a local module extension whose use_repo calls disagree with its
extension_metadata, defined in this script), and compares exit code, stdout and
stderr byte for byte. For `tidy` cases the resulting MODULE.bazel is compared too.

How each command runs (as scripts/oracle/record and scripts/w4a/run do): cwd is the work copy
~/.cache/blaze/work/mod-compare/<side>/<project> (rsync of ~/.cache/blaze/corpus/<project>
minus bazel-* and .git; refreshed at the start and before and after every tidy case); env -i HOME,
PATH=/usr/bin:/bin; startup --output_user_root=~/.cache/blaze/oracle-out/mod-compare-<side>
--nohome_rc --nosystem_rc; command options --repository_cache=~/.cache/blaze/repo-cache
--color=no --curses=no; under systemd-run --scope MemoryMax=12G MemorySwapMax=0. Before the
cases each side runs one discarded `mod graph` (fetches the module graph and the repositories
it needs into the output base). The oracle's server is shut down before every case, so each
case runs in a new server as every Blaze command does (a server that already evaluated a
module extension does not repeat its warnings), and at the end.

Comparison: byte for byte after replacing, on each side, its own output user root with <OUR>,
its work copy with <WS>, and 32-hex-digit directory names directly under <OUR> and
<OUR>/install with <MD5> (output base and install base names differ between the two binaries
and work copies), and dropping a leading "Starting local Bazel server (9.3.2) and connecting to
it..." line from stderr (Blaze has no persistent server and prints it on every command; the
oracle prints it only in the discarded warm-up). The table says "raw" when the bytes were
identical even before that. --side none only re-compares captured files.

Output: one line per case (MATCH / DIFF with the differing parts / DIFF-UI when the only
difference is in stderr and disappears without the UI's timing-dependent " no actions running"
progress lines and the newline UiEventHandler.completeBuild adds after stdout that did not end
in one; both are UI code outside `mod`), a summary line; the captured
files are in ~/.cache/blaze/work/mod-compare/results/<side>/<project>/<case>.{rc,out,err,module}.
--show NAME prints a unified diff of one case (project/case).

Guards (scripts/lib/compare_common.py): every command runs under a supervisor in the scope that
records how it really ended (`exit N`, `signal NAME`, `oom-kill`, `timeout` after 3600 s), kept
in <case>.term; the comparison uses it (<case>.rc is for reading only; a capture without .term
never matches). The oracle must be the pinned one (UPSTREAM.json). Each oracle capture has
<case>.key (oracle sha256, this tool's sha256, the argv and environment, the digest of the corpus
checkout, the project and the cases before it); --side blaze and --side none refuse a stored
oracle capture whose key differs from this run's. Classes: IDENTICAL (MATCH; the oracle exited
0, or DECLARED_EXIT names the case with that exit code), DIFFERENT (DIFF and DIFF-UI),
BOTH-FAILED (equal failures not declared), NOT-PORTED, ORACLE-UNEXPECTED, SKIPPED (MISSING). The
output starts with the repository HEAD and dirty flag and both binaries' paths and sha256, and
ends with the denominator; --json writes the report. Exit 0 only when at least one case was
compared and every selected case is IDENTICAL; 1 otherwise (an empty selection included); 2 on
a refusal.
"""

